  "result": "If I could change the world in exactly one way, I\u2019d give every single person the gift of genuine, lived empathy\u2014that intuitive capacity to feel what others feel and to see oneself in their shoes. Not just polite understanding, but a deep, involuntary resonance with another\u2019s joy and suffering.\n\nWhy that one change?\n\n  \u2022 It would dissolve the walls between \u201cus\u201d and \u201cthem,\u201d making conflict far harder to justify.  \n  \u2022 It would turn random charity into sustained solidarity: people would instinctively act for the long-term well-being of strangers.  \n  \u2022 It would reframe our relationship with the planet, since harming ecosystems or nonhuman lives would feel like harming ourselves.  \n  \u2022 It would strengthen communities, because cooperation would feel as natural as breathing.  \n\nWith universal empathy as our starting point, nearly every other global challenge\u2014inequality, violence, environmental collapse\u2014becomes surmountable. In a world where we truly feel each other\u2019s hopes and pains, compassion wouldn\u2019t be an aspiration: it would be automatic.",
